<%# Server-rendered "jukebox is closed" screen. Used when the jukebox has no live
    player (guest opened a closed jukebox, or the host stopped the music). Rendered
    in plain ERB on purpose: the name goes through normal HTML escaping (which the
    browser decodes correctly), so there's none of the JS-string round-trip /
    device-cache fragility the React closed view had. Styled by ajb.css. %>
<div id="ajb-guest-root" class="ajb">
  <div class="ajb-closed">
    <div class="ajb-closed-emoji">🎉</div>
    <h1><%= @jukebox.name %> is closed</h1>
    <p class="ajb-muted">Thanks for coming! 👋</p>
    <p class="ajb-muted ajb-small">
      The host stopped the music. If they start it back up, just reload this page to rejoin.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
